# PeerLearn: Concept and Tools

## Project idea

- **Name:** PeerLearn
- **One line:** A platform where students explain concepts they understand to their classmates.

## The problem

- Students often do not understand a topic from lectures or slides alone.
- Good explanations by classmates stay inside private chats and are lost afterwards.
- There is no single place to search, rate and ask questions about student explanations.
- Revising before exams takes a lot of time because the material is scattered.

## The solution

- An explainer writes a clear explanation of a concept they studied.
- Classmates search by topic or subject, read the explanation and rate it.
- Students ask questions under an explanation and the explainer answers.
- AI generates a short summary and a practice quiz from each explanation.
- Top rated and most viewed explanations are easy to find.
- An admin manages subjects, removes inappropriate content and views usage statistics.

## Target audience

- **Students:** search, read, rate, ask questions and use the AI summary and quiz.
- **Explainers:** students who write explanations and answer questions.
- **Admins:** teaching assistants or team members who manage subjects and content.
- University students in any course, starting with computer science.

## Tech stack

| Area | Tool |
|---|---|
| Language | Python |
| User interface | Streamlit |
| Database | SQLite (sqlite3 module) |
| Data analysis and charts | pandas, Streamlit charts |
| AI features | An LLM API for summaries and quizzes |
| Password security | bcrypt |
| Testing | pytest |
| Version control | Git and GitHub |
| Editor | VS Code |
| Backlog and planning | GitHub Issues and GitHub Projects (board) |
| Diagrams | PlantUML |
| AI coding assistant | Replit Agent or similar (vibe coding) |

## Team roles

- **AI:** summaries, quizzes and prompts.
- **Data analysis:** ratings, rankings, dashboard and database design.
- **UI/UX:** screens, navigation and user experience.
